{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-164474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}-(z-1)^{2}=1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperboloid of one sheet with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(-1,3,1),\\,a=b=c=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets"] ["text" "A sphere"] ["text" "An ellipsoid"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of one sheet"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-(z-2)^{2}=-1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperboloid of two sheets with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(-1,0,2),\\,a=\\sqrt{3},\\,b=2,\\,c=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets"] ["text" "An ellipsoid"] ["text" "An elliptic cone"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of two sheets"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=8y,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder, whose axis is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a parabolic cylinder with $p=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A couple of incident planes"] ["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder"] ["text" "A paraboloid"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164480" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parabolic cylinder"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty \n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ in the $xy$-plane, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(-2,1),\\,a=b=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid"] ["text" "A hyperboloid"] ["text" "An elliptic cone"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbolic cylinder"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}=-y,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty \n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder, whose axis is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py,\n$$\n\nand a parabolic cylinder, shifted ${x}_{0}$ along the x-axis and ${y}_{0}$ along the y-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}=4p(y-{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a parabolic cylinder with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(-2,0),\\,p=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder"] ["text" "A plane"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164482" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parabolic cylinder"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=-12y,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis and $p=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A couple of planes"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $x=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, an elliptic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is an elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=\\sqrt{2},\\,c=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${z}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $a=b=c=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis and $a=1,\\,b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164507" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, an elliptic cone centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is an elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $a=1,\\,b=c=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid with one sheet whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2x+20y+11 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+5({y}^{2}+4y)+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5([y+2)^{2}-4]+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+5(y+2)^{2}-20+{z}^{2}+11 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+5(y+2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,-2,0)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,2,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,-2,0)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,2,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164555" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,-2,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12x+8y-10=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12x+8y-10 & =0 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-2x)-4({y}^{2}-2y)-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-6-4(y-1)^{2}+4-6{z}^{2}-10 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)^{2}-4(y-1)^{2}-6{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A ellipsoid centered at $(1,1,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,-1,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,1,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(-1,-1,0)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36666" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,1,0)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $4{y}^{2}+8y+9{z}^{2}-5x+9=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $y$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}+8y+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4({y}^{2}+2y)+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4[(y+1)^{2}-1]+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}-4+9{z}^{2}-5x+9 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2}-5x+5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2}-5x+5 & =0 \\\\ 4(y+1)^{2}+9{z}^{2} & =5(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{4(y+1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{9{z}^{2}}{5} & =x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,-1,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,0,1)$"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,-1,0)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,-1,0)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(-1,1,0)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,-1,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,-1,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-2y-8z-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-({y}^{2}+2y)+2({z}^{2}-4z)-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2[(z-2)^{2}-4]-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+1+2(z-2)^{2}-8-9 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-(y+1)^{2}+2(z-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A ellipsoid centered at $(0,-1,2)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,1,2)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(0,-1,-2)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(0,-1,2)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-164550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(0,-1,2)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12y-z+13=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $y$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12y-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3({y}^{2}+4y)-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3[(y+2)^{2}-4]-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-12-z+13 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-z+1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2}-z+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y+2)^{2} & =z-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2add8b7fae46e751342683e029a53f1f5e99cc56cb1bacf0106b7a69a483c496"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(0,-2,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,-2,0)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,-2,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "q-36111" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(0,-2,1)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/state.json" "file_sha256" "72cbf30df9d57b70e34778c201bb3795b41193980b5382a9b182b5f1a2170562"} {"question" "e-12559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $z -1 = \\dfrac{(x-3)^2}{4} - \\dfrac{(y+2)^2}4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-12559.json" "file_sha256" "c2c60041a1c839108b4003058d784596738e25a11715b1cd70ce7cbd99c5551d"} {"question" "e-12559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2},\n$$\n\nand a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2}.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n(x_0,y_0,z_0) = (3, -2, 1), \\quad a= b=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-12559.json" "file_sha256" "c2c60041a1c839108b4003058d784596738e25a11715b1cd70ce7cbd99c5551d"} {"question" "e-12560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $x = \\dfrac{y^2}{4} - 4z^2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-12560.json" "file_sha256" "fd1808a8660edab4831a6b5598b0851e1000acd26b4c0d59db5a45fe04fb7f5d"} {"question" "e-12560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $\\boldsymbol x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} - \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis, and $b=2, \\: c=\\dfrac 12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-12560.json" "file_sha256" "fd1808a8660edab4831a6b5598b0851e1000acd26b4c0d59db5a45fe04fb7f5d"} {"question" "e-8313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $-x^2 + z^2 + 2x + y=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-8313.json" "file_sha256" "54af36f7249cc617fd5b1e52f6cf8f3df74f42fb93de456717b975f517c8cc75"} {"question" "e-8313" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}+2x+y & =0 \\\\ -({x}^{2}-2x)+{z}^{2}+y & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)^{2}+1+{z}^{2}+y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x-1)^{2}+1+{z}^{2}+y & =0 \\\\ -(x-1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =-y-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-{z}^{2} & =y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1, -1, 0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042813/example-8313.json" "file_sha256" "54af36f7249cc617fd5b1e52f6cf8f3df74f42fb93de456717b975f517c8cc75"}] "usage" {"e-12560" [] "e-8313" [] "q-164373" [] "e-12559" []} "basis" 1581 "retractions" [[17592186124749 :question/problem "Identify the surface $z^{2} + y^{2} - x^{2} = 1$."] [17592186124132 :question/problem "Identify the surface $z -1 = \\dfrac{(x-3)^2}{4} - \\dfrac{(y+2)^2}4$."] [17592186124132 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}\n$$\n\nand a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ is given by\n\n$$\nz - z_0 = \\dfrac{(x-x_0)^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{(y-y_0)^2}{b^2}\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n(x_0,y_0,z_0) = (3, -2, 1), \\quad a= b=2\n$$"] [17592186124133 :question/problem "Identify the surface $x = \\dfrac{y^2}{4} - 4z^2$."] [17592186124133 :question/worked-solution "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nz = \\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}-\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $O$ whose axis of symmetry is the $\\boldsymbol x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2} - \\dfrac{z^2}{c^2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic paraboloid whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis, and\n\n$$\nb=2, \\: c=\\dfrac 12\n$$"] [17592186124327 :question/problem "Identify the surface $-x^2 + z^2 + 2x + y=0$."] [17592186124327 :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square in the $x$ term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x^{2} + z^{2} + 2x + y &= 0 \\\\\n- (x^{2} - 2x) + z^{2} + y &= 0 \\\\\n- (x - 1)^{2} + 1 + z^{2} + y &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- (x - 1)^{2} + 1 + z^{2} + y &= 0 \\\\\n- (x - 1)^{2} + z^{2} &= -y - 1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} - z^{2} &= y + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1, -1, 0)$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121514 17592186121515 17592186121516 17592186121517 17592186121518] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121513 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121513 :answer-field/id] [17592186121513 :answer-field/key] [17592186121513 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
